# Applies to a build whose context is the repository root, which backend-java is: it builds one
# leaf of the Maven reactor and needs the parent pom beside it.  Every other service names its
# own subdirectory, and backend/ and spark/ carry their own .dockerignore.  Without this file a
# root-context build uploads the working tree: .git alone is over a gigabyte here, because the
# Git LFS object store lives inside it.
.git
# A host build's output.  Copying it in would put a jar built against the host's JDK beside the
# one the image builds, and Maven would then decide which of the two to use.
target
**/target
.github
.claude
# Another service's vendored artefacts.  This build needs htap-cqlite/dist, which is 78.3 MB and
# is copied in the Dockerfile; the other three are 511.2 MB of Sidecar tarball, 41.8 MB of Python
# wheels and 176.5 MB of Ivy jars, of which 126.6 MB is one cassandra-analytics-core.  A
# root-context build uploads all three unless they are named here, and spark/'s own .dockerignore
# does not apply, because that one governs a build whose context is spark/.
backend/dist
cassandra/dist
spark/ivy
cassandra-data
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
docs
workshop
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.venv
venv
.ci-tmp
.DS_Store
*.swp
